{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"59a7ff09790c53b2","name":"card_unit_lublin_r_xiii","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Poland/units/card_unit_lublin_r_xiii","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"LUBLIN R-XIII","text":"Cards you play have Intel 1.\r\nDeployment: Reveal target Covert unit.","flavorText":"The Lublin R-XIII was a reconnaissance and light bomber aircraft primarily used by the Polish Air Force during WWII, particularly in the early stages of the conflict. The Polish aircraft manufacturer Plage i Laśkiewicz built the aircraft in the 1930s and it proved to be an effective asset for its purpose. On the eve of the Invasion of Poland in 1939, the Polish Air Force had about 150 R-XIII at their disposal, but only 49 of them were combat ready. The rest were in reserve, used for training purposes or in repairs. The R-XIII turned out to be inferior to all Luftwaffe aircraft, including fighters, bombers, and reconnaissance planes, due to its slower speed and limited armament consisting of just one machine gun. However, it proved itself useful in close reconnaissance and liaison duties and was actively employed in these roles. A total of 273 Lublin R-XIII were built, including a few variants, and none have survived until today.","faction":"Poland","type":"fighter","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_lublin_r_xiii","title":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_lublin_r_xiii_title","SourceString":"LUBLIN R-XIII","LocalizedString":"LUBLIN R-XIII"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":2,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Poland","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_lublin_r_xiii_text","SourceString":"Cards you play have Intel 1.\r\nDeployment: Reveal target Covert unit.","LocalizedString":"Cards you play have Intel 1.\r\nDeployment: Reveal target Covert unit."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_lublin_r_xiii_history","SourceString":"The Lublin R-XIII was a reconnaissance and light bomber aircraft primarily used by the Polish Air Force during WWII, particularly in the early stages of the conflict. The Polish aircraft manufacturer Plage i Laśkiewicz built the aircraft in the 1930s and it proved to be an effective asset for its purpose. On the eve of the Invasion of Poland in 1939, the Polish Air Force had about 150 R-XIII at their disposal, but only 49 of them were combat ready. The rest were in reserve, used for training purposes or in repairs. The R-XIII turned out to be inferior to all Luftwaffe aircraft, including fighters, bombers, and reconnaissance planes, due to its slower speed and limited armament consisting of just one machine gun. However, it proved itself useful in close reconnaissance and liaison duties and was actively employed in these roles. A total of 273 Lublin R-XIII were built, including a few variants, and none have survived until today.","LocalizedString":"The Lublin R-XIII was a reconnaissance and light bomber aircraft primarily used by the Polish Air Force during WWII, particularly in the early stages of the conflict. The Polish aircraft manufacturer Plage i Laśkiewicz built the aircraft in the 1930s and it proved to be an effective asset for its purpose. On the eve of the Invasion of Poland in 1939, the Polish Air Force had about 150 R-XIII at their disposal, but only 49 of them were combat ready. The rest were in reserve, used for training purposes or in repairs. The R-XIII turned out to be inferior to all Luftwaffe aircraft, including fighters, bombers, and reconnaissance planes, due to its slower speed and limited armament consisting of just one machine gun. However, it proved itself useful in close reconnaissance and liaison duties and was actively employed in these roles. A total of 273 Lublin R-XIII were built, including a few variants, and none have survived until today."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","s